.\"
.Dd $Mdocdate: October 18 2026 $
.Dt SLMON 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slmon
.Nd Starlink dish monitor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm slmon
.Ar command
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl d Ar db
.Op Fl l Ar host:port
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
records samples from a Starlink dish and a few local health signals,
and serves them on its HTTP listener.
It is an unofficial monitor.
It is not a SpaceX program and it does not speak for the dish operator.
.Pp
The dish protocol is the public Device Handle service.
.Pp
The intended dish is bridged onto an
.Ox
firewall.
The default dish address is
.Li 192.168.100.1
port 9200.
A host with no route to that address must set
.Va dish_host
or add a route before live samples will appear.
.Nm once
prints a one-line refusal and returns when that port does not answer.
.Pp
.Ar command
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width status
.It Cm start
Run the monitor in the foreground until
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Dv SIGINT ,
or
.Dv SIGHUP .
The first start against an empty database prompts for an admin user and
password when standard input is a terminal.
.It Cm init
Prompt for the admin user and password, store them, and exit.
A second
.Cm init
prints that the database is already initialized and does not change the
password.
.It Cm status
Print whether the database is initialized, which driver is configured,
the dish host, the HTTP port, and how many history samples are stored.
This opens the database read-only in a separate process.
.It Cm once
Probe the dish once and print one status document as JSON.
This does not start the daemon and does not write the database.
.El
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file
Read configuration from
.Ar file .
The file is
.Li key = value
lines.
Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.Ql #
are ignored.
Unknown keys are rejected.
.It Fl d Ar db
SQLite database file.
Overrides
.Ev SLMON_DB
and the default path.
The directory of this file also holds
.Pa http.port .
.It Fl l Ar host:port
HTTP listen address.
Overrides the
.Va listen
key.
Port 0 asks the kernel for a free port; the chosen port is written to
.Pa http.port .
.El
.Sh PROCESSES
.Nm
follows the shape of an
.Ox
.Xr imsg_init 3
daemon.
The parent forks the children and restarts a child that exits.
If the database child exits, the parent kills the others and exits
non-zero so that
.Xr rc 8
can restart the whole monitor.
A child that dies within two seconds of starting is restarted after a
one-second pause.
.Pp
Process titles are
.Li slmon: parent ,
.Li slmon: dish ,
.Li slmon: db ,
.Li slmon: http ,
.Li slmon: watchdog ,
and, when coordinates are configured,
.Li slmon: weather .
Each child is pledged to the promises it needs.
The parent keeps a wider pledge so a restarted child can still narrow
itself, including
.Xr unveil 2 .
.Bl -tag -width watchdog
.It parent
Supervises children.
It does not open the database.
.It dish
The only process that loads
.Li libgrpc++ .
It is forked before that library is loaded, and it never forks again.
Every
.Va dish_interval_s
seconds (default 30) it calls
.Fn get_status
and
.Fn get_history .
The history ring is one sample per second.
The obstruction map is fetched every five minutes.
Each RPC deadline is five seconds.
The channel is plaintext on port 9200.
If that port does not answer, the child logs that once and tries again
on the next interval.
It keeps running.
.It db
The only process that writes the database.
Other processes send it messages and read rows back the same way.
.It http
Serves the loopback HTTP API.
The parent binds the listen socket and passes it in, so a restarted
HTTP process keeps the same port.
.It watchdog
Runs
.Xr ping 8
.Fl n Fl c Cm 1 Fl w Cm 2
against
.Va ping_targets .
Three failures in a row record a disconnect.
A later success records how long the disconnect lasted.
A latency spike is the best round-trip time above
.Va spike_ms
for at least
.Va spike_min_s .
.It weather
Started only when both
.Va latitude
and
.Va longitude
are set.
It reads the Open-Meteo forecast over HTTPS.
Sending those warnings onward is not implemented.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Keys and their defaults:
.Bl -tag -width "minutely_retention_days"
.It Va listen
.Li 127.0.0.1:8080 .
Must be
.Li host:port .
.It Va dish_host
.Li 192.168.100.1 .
A suffix
.Li :port
replaces the default port 9200.
.It Va dish_interval_s
.Li 30 .
Minimum 1.
.It Va db
.Li sqlite
or
.Li pg .
.It Va pg_host , Va pg_port , Va pg_db , Va pg_user , Va pg_password
PostgreSQL connection.
.Va pg_host
is the directory of the local socket when it begins with a slash.
.Va db No = Li pg
requires
.Va pg_db .
.It Va latitude , Va longitude
Decimal degrees.
Set both or neither.
Setting both starts the weather process.
.It Va raw_retention_days
.Li 90 .
Raw history and status rows older than this are folded into hourly rows
and then deleted.
.It Va hourly_rollup_days
.Li 365 .
Hourly rows older than this are folded into daily rows and then deleted.
.It Va minutely_retention_days
.Li 730 .
Per-minute rows older than this are deleted.
.It Va rollup_interval_s
.Li 60 .
How often completed minutes, hours, and days are rolled up.
Minimum 1.
.It Va ping_targets
.Li 1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 .
Comma-separated hosts.
.It Va ping_interval_s
.Li 10 .
.It Va disconnect_failures
.Li 3 .
.It Va spike_ms
.Li 200 .
.It Va spike_min_s
.Li 30 .
.El
.Pp
A sample file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
listen = 127.0.0.1:8080
dish_host = 192.168.100.1
dish_interval_s = 30
db = sqlite
.Ed
.Pp
PostgreSQL instead of SQLite:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
db = pg
pg_db = slmon
pg_user = slmon
pg_host = /var/run/postgresql
.Ed
.Sh FIRST START
.Cm init ,
or
.Cm start
on a terminal, asks:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Admin user [admin]:
Password:
Repeat password:
.Ed
.Pp
An empty user name stores
.Li admin .
The password is read with echo off, must be at least 8 characters, and
must be entered the same way twice.
It is stored with
.Xr crypt 3
bcrypt
.Pq Li $2b$ .
A 32-byte session key is read from
.Pa /dev/urandom
once and reused on later starts.
.Pp
.Cm start
with no password stored, and with standard input not a terminal, exits
with the message:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
slmon: no admin password is set. Run `slmon init` or `slmon start` from a terminal.
.Ed
.Pp
A later
.Cm start
does not prompt again.
.Sh HTTP
The listener is one request per connection, with
.Li Connection: close
and a five-second read timeout.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /
With no session, redirects to
.Pa /login .
With a session, returns the dashboard: the latest sample, charts, the
obstruction grid, and recent events.
.Va range
is
.Li 1h ,
.Li 6h
.Pq the default ,
.Li 24h ,
or
.Li 7d .
One hour is drawn from status polls.
Six and 24 hours use the per-minute rollup.
Seven days uses the hourly rollup.
The obstruction chart uses status polls for every range.
A logout button posts to
.Pa /logout .
.It Cm GET /login
The login form.
A browser posts it to
.Pa /login .
.It Cm POST /login
The same user and password fields as
.Pa /api/login .
Success sets the cookie and redirects to
.Pa / .
Failure renders the form again.
.It Cm POST /logout
Clears the cookie and redirects to
.Pa /login .
.It Cm GET /health
Open.
Returns a small JSON object.
No cookie is required.
.It Cm POST /api/login
JSON or form body with
.Va user
.Pq or Va username
and
.Va password .
Success sets the cookie
.Va slmon_session
for 12 hours,
.Li HttpOnly ,
.Li SameSite=Lax .
Five failures from one address in five minutes are rejected.
A success clears that counter.
The password hash stays in the database process.
.It Cm POST /api/logout
Clears the cookie.
.It Cm GET /api/latest/ Ns Ar table
The newest row of an allowed table.
Requires the admin session cookie.
.It Cm GET /api/raw/ Ns Ar table Ns ?from&to&limit&order
Rows in a time range.
.Va limit
defaults to 5000 and is clamped to 50000.
.Va order
is
.Li asc
or
.Li desc .
.El
.Pp
Allowed tables are
.Li history_samples ,
.Li metrics ,
.Li metrics_minutely ,
.Li metrics_hourly ,
.Li metrics_daily ,
.Li events ,
.Li dish_info ,
.Li obstruction_map ,
.Li weather ,
.Li speedtests ,
and
.Li alert_queue .
There is no delete request.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ./var/slmon.db
Default SQLite file when
.Nm
is run from a checkout that contains
.Pa lib/SLMON.pm .
Mode 0600.
SQLite is used in WAL mode.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/slmon/slmon.db
Default SQLite file otherwise.
.It Pa http.port
Text file next to the SQLite database, holding the HTTP port.
.It Pa /etc/slmon.conf
Path used by the sample
.Pa rc.d/slmon
script.
That script is an example; its
.Va daemon
path must be edited before install.
.El
.Pp
.Ev SLMON_DB
selects the SQLite file when
.Fl d
is not given.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm start
runs until a signal.
It exits non-zero if the database child dies or if it is started
non-interactively before a password has been set.
.Cm init
exits non-zero if the prompt cannot be read.
.Cm status
exits non-zero when the database cannot be opened.
.Cm once
exits 0 after printing status JSON, and also exits 0 when the dish port
does not answer.
The refusal is printed on standard error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr crypt 3 ,
.Xr imsg_init 3 ,
.Xr ping 8 ,
.Xr rc 8
